gpu_thread: wake for submissions during semaphore waits

From viejunerd's Eglantine-PS5 patch 0041 (tag v1.219.012). next12 left it out, because
it calls PopWaitFor, which our Common::HostCommandQueue from patch 0028 does not have:
that was the compile error of CI run 42080309459.

While a channel waits on a semaphore the GPU thread polled for 500 us and then slept 1 ms
at a time, so a command list arriving meanwhile waited out the rest of the sleep. It now
waits on the queue for 250 us at a time, polling the semaphores in between, because a
release is a plain guest memory write that wakes nothing.

Changed from the patch: PopWaitFor goes on HostCommandQueue instead of SPSCQueue, which
the GPU thread no longer uses. Waits on the queue's mutex and condition variable, as
PopWait does; TryEmplace notifies after unlocking, and the predicate is checked under
the mutex, so no wake-up is lost.

The port's rewrites of gpu_thread.cpp in headless/CMakeLists.txt do not touch this block.

